This file is a single Streamlit app with 2 functions and many configuration/runtime variables.

Functions

1) decode_qr_payload_to_dt(hex_str: str)
- Purpose: reverse-decodes the 12-character hex QR payload into a Python datetime.
- Input:
  - hex_str: a 12-character hex string, representing 6 bytes
- Behavior:
  - Validates length is exactly 12 characters
  - Splits into 6 bytes
  - Applies the custom inverse math to recover:
    - year = 2000 + Y
    - month M
    - day D
    - hour H
    - minute m
    - second s
  - Returns a datetime.datetime object
- Error handling:
  - Raises ValueError if the payload length is invalid

2) calibrate_from_github_cached(url: str, start_date: datetime.date)
- Purpose: calibrates the device’s timing drift and base minute/second by reading example reference logs and fitting a linear model.
- Decorator:
  - @st.cache_data
  - so the results are cached by Streamlit
- Behavior:
  - Tries to read reference data from a local file reference, or falls back to fetching it from GitHub
  - Parses lines that look like:
    - YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM ... @HEX12
  - Converts each QR payload to a datetime via decode_qr_payload_to_dt()
  - Compares observed vs decoded times relative to the provided start date
  - Performs a simple linear regression on:
    - x = elapsed days
    - y = seconds within the hour
  - Returns:
    - base_minute
    - base_second
    - drift_per_day
- Fallback if no valid calibration data exists:
  - returns (10, 0.0, -0.45)

Important variables

Imports / module objects
- datetime
  - Python datetime library used for date/time math
- io
  - for in-memory PNG buffer generation
- re
  - regex parsing of reference log lines
- urllib.request
  - handles HTTP fetching from GitHub
- qrcode
  - creates QR codes
- Image
  - from PIL, for image transpose/rotation
- st
  - Streamlit app object
- os
  - file path handling

Constants
- BASE_MHZ = 16.0
  - unused constant in this file
- LOCAL_REF_PATH = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "reference")
  - local path to the reference calibration file
- REF_URL = "https://githubusercontent.com"
  - base URL used for reference data lookup

Session state keys
These are stored in st.session_state:

- "hour_offset"
  - integer hour offset for testing different time slots
- "start_date"
  - base date from which elapsed days are measured
  - initialized to datetime.date(2025, 8, 1)
- "rtc_readout_offset_sec"
  - offset in seconds added to RTC-derived time
- "real_wakeup_offset_min"
  - offset in minutes for the real-world switch boundary
- "qr_version"
  - QR version setting; 0 means auto
- "qr_ec"
  - error correction level: "L", "M", "Q", or "H"
- "qr_box_size"
  - QR module size in pixels
- "qr_mask"
  - mask pattern, or -1 to auto
- "qr_transpose"
  - boolean; whether to transpose the QR image diagonally

Calibration-related variables inside calibrate_from_github_cached
- lines
  - read reference file content split into lines
- records
  - list of parsed calibration observations
- start_dt
  - start of the calibration window as midnight on start_date
- m_obj
  - regex match object for each line
- obs_dt
  - observed datetime from the log
- hex_str
  - 12-char QR payload from the log
- dev_dt
  - decoded QR datetime
- days
  - elapsed days from start_dt
- sec_in_hour
  - number of seconds past the minute mark
- n
  - number of valid records
- sum_x, sum_y, sum_xy, sum_xx
  - regression sums
- denominator
  - denominator for the slope calculation
- drift_per_day
  - fitted drift rate in seconds/day
- intercept
  - fitted base seconds value
- base_minute
  - integer minute portion of intercept
- base_second
  - remaining seconds portion of intercept

Main app runtime variables
These are created after initialization and drive the QR generation:

- EC_MAP
  - maps error-correction letters to qrcode constants
- hkt
  - timezone object for Hong Kong Time (UTC+8)
- now_hkt
  - current datetime in HKT
- adjusted_now
  - now_hkt plus hour_offset
- start_dt
  - start_date at midnight in HKT
- temp_slot_start
  - adjusted_now rounded down to the start of the current hour
- elapsed_days
  - number of days from start_dt to temp_slot_start
- current_rtc_drift_sec
  - RTC drift in seconds, based on elapsed_days * fitted_drift
- total_rtc_offset_sec
  - RTC drift + rtc_readout_offset_sec
- rtc_offset_min
  - total_rtc_offset_sec / 60
- total_span_days
  - constant: 469.5
- boundary_rate
  - computed switch boundary rate: -15 / total_span_days
- raw_boundary_exact
  - exact boundary minute value
- rounded_boundary
  - rounded raw boundary
- boundary_minute
  - boundary expressed as minute-of-hour
- switch_display
  - safety-formatted string showing the real-world switch boundary
- base_hour_slot
  - adjusted_now at the top of the hour
- boundary_dt
  - exact datetime of the boundary for the current hour
- slot_start
  - selected active slot start time
- effective_time
  - computed effective datetime used for QR payload generation

Payload / output variables
- Y, M, D, H, m, s
  - year, month, day, hour, minute, second of effective_time
- b0, b1, b2, b3, b4, b5
  - six bytes encoded into the QR payload
- decoded_src
  - tuple of (Y, M, D, H, m, s)
- hex_payload
  - final 12-character hexadecimal payload
- qr_message
  - string like:
    - checkin://q?91/@<hex_payload>
- target_version
  - chosen QR version, or None for auto
- target_mask
  - chosen mask pattern, or None for auto
- qr
  - qrcode.QRCode instance
- img
  - generated QR image
- buf
  - in-memory PNG buffer

UI display variables
- offset_label
  - text showing the hour offset in the caption
- ver_label
  - either "Auto" or Vn
- actual_mask
  - actual mask pattern used by qrcode
- mask_label
  - formatted display string for mask setting
- trans_label
  - text for transpose state

There are no classes in this file; it is a procedural Streamlit script.
